WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.867
Matplotlib.

2
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:04.809
The real way to use it is its object model.

3
00:00:04.809 --> 00:00:08.067
Let's meet the pieces, starting with the page itself.

4
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.700
Matplotlib has a simple hierarchy.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.300
The Figure is the canvas, the whole page.

6
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.300
Each Axes is one plot living on that figure.

7
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.500
And every line, label, legend, and title hangs off an Axes.

8
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:23.900
There are two styles.

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.833
The plt dot plot state machine is fine for a throwaway.

10
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.233
But it relies on hidden global state.

11
00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:34.067
The Axes API is explicit, and gives you full control.

12
00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.600
Use it when it matters.

13
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.367
Here's a learning curve in code.

14
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:42.033
One call to subplots hands you the figure and the axes.

15
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:45.800
We plot training and validation loss on the same axes.

16
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.667
Then we label the axes and add a legend.

17
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:52.800
And save the figure as an image, at a hundred and fifty dots per inch.

18
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.300
Here's why this matters.

19
00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.267
You plot train and validation loss on the same Axes after every run.

20
00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:05.600
Around epoch twelve, validation loss starts rising while training keeps falling.

21
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.250
The picture says overfitting faster than any metric table.

22
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.200
These numbers are illustrative.

23
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.600
One more benefit.

24
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:19.667
Because the plot is scripted with the Axes API, every experiment gets the same styling.

25
00:01:19.967 --> 00:01:21.633
All fifty plots look alike.

26
00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:24.367
So they're instantly comparable in your run log.

27
00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.322
Let's recap.

28
00:01:26.322 --> 00:01:29.467
The Figure is the canvas and the Axes is the plot.

29
00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:31.333
Subplots returns both.

30
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:33.933
Use the Axes API for control.

31
00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:36.454
And savefig makes the artifact.

32
00:01:36.454 --> 00:01:37.600
Next up: Plotly.
